{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":7973428,"ns":0,"title":"Anfinsen's dogma","extract":"Anfinsen's dogma, also known as the thermodynamic hypothesis, is a postulate in molecular biology. It states that, at least for a small globular protein in its standard physiological environment, the native structure is determined only by the protein's amino acid sequence.","description":"Molecular biology hypothesis","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}